# A wheel of radius radius rolls right without slipping.
# Its center advances radius*t while it turns clockwise through t radians.
# A pen at distance offset from the center traces the amber trochoid.
# Set offset = radius to make a cycloid, offset < radius for a curtate curve,
# or offset > radius for loops. The latter pen lies outside the wheel.
# Predict when the pen's horizontal velocity radius-offset*cos(t) is negative.
# At offset = radius, both velocity components vanish at contact: a cusp forms.
# Drag t to inspect those moments, or play the animation for two revolutions.
# The trace is sampled: a sharp cusp's appearance depends on display resolution.
scene "Rolling wheel: the geometry of a trochoid";
coordinates equal;
domain -2.5 20;
range -2 4;
param radius = 1 from 0.6 to 1.4;
param offset = 1 from 0 to 1.8;
param t = 0 from 0 to 12.566370614359172;
animate t from 0 to 12.566370614359172 duration 12;
parametric trace(x) = (radius*x-offset*sin(x),radius-offset*cos(x)) from 0 to 12.566370614359172 color amber;
parametric wheel(x) = (radius*t+radius*cos(x),radius+radius*sin(x)) from 0 to 6.283185307179586 color blue;
segment ground from (-2.5,0) to (20,0) color white;
segment spoke from (radius*t,radius) to (radius*t-offset*sin(t),radius-offset*cos(t)) color rose;
point center = (radius*t,radius) color blue;
point pen = (radius*t-offset*sin(t),radius-offset*cos(t)) color rose;
point contact = (radius*t,0) color teal;
